# BW-2001 (Machine 130): the PET 2001's board, laid out after PET-Shack's "PET CPU BOARD"
# drawing (docs/p5q1-bw2001-board/BW2001_BOARD.md). Columns J (left) to A (right), rows 9 (the
# back) to 1 (the front); most chips lie with the notch at the left, the big ones stand upright.
grid pet
upright UF3 down            # the 6502, notch at the bottom (the drawing's F1)
upright UG8 down 0          # PIA1, notch at the top (G6)
upright UG9 in 0            # the 74LS145 ("GH"), pin 1 top left
upright UB8 down            # PIA2 (B7)
upright UA5 down            # the VIA (A3)
upright UG2 down            # the 74154 (G1, no notch drawn)
upright UE6 up              # the 74100 (E5)
upright UA2 up              # the character ROM (A2)

# The PET's edge connectors down the right edge; power, cassette #1, the keyboard header, the
# LED and the monitor along the back.
edge J1 right 17%           # IEEE-488, beside UA7-UA9 (rows 9-7)
edge J2 right 50%           # user port, beside the VIA
edge J3 right 90%           # cassette #2, by UA1
edge J8 back 10%            # power, over columns I-H
edge J6 back 20%            # cassette #1
edge J5 back 40%            # keyboard: inside the board by columns H-G on the PET
edge DS1 back 55%           # the diagnostic LED, by column E
edge J7 back 66%            # monitor, by column D

# Pull-ups beside the chips whose pins they hold, chained along a row's resistor band, away from
# the upright chips.
next R29 UE3 front          # BA1-BA5 (row 3, columns E-C: UF3 stands in column F)
next R30 R29 right
next R31 R30 right
next R32 R31 right
next R33 R32 right
next R34 UE4 front          # BA6-BA10 (row 4)
next R35 R34 right
next R36 R35 right
next R37 R36 right
next R38 R37 right
next R25 UG8 front          # KIN7-KIN0, the keyboard columns (row 7, columns G-J)
next R24 R25 left
next R23 R24 left
next R22 R23 left
next R21 R22 left
next R20 R21 left
next R19 R20 left
next R18 R19 left
next R28 UE2 front          # BA0
next R46 R28 right          # the clock gate's enable
next R13 UF3 front          # NMI_N, RDY, IRQ_N
next R14 R13 right
next R17 R14 right
next R10 UA9 front          # IFC_N, EOI_N
next R48 R10 left
next R26 UG3 front          # spare inputs of UG3, UG4
next R12 UC7 front          # the flip-flops' J, K and clears
next R39 UC5 front
next R40 UD2 front
next R41 UB6 front
next R43 UA1 front
next R44 UC1 front
next R45 R44 right
next R27 UE8 front
